---
description: Never self-certify a deliverable — have an independent subagent review and test it from scratch before reporting done.
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `independent-review`:

1. Before reporting any deliverable done, spawn ONE independent subagent with the ORIGINAL requirements and checkable acceptance criteria — not your summary of them.
2. Instruct it to verify from scratch: re-run tests, re-read code, re-check live state. Report only what was independently verified, with evidence. A spawn receipt is not a review.
3. If it disagrees with you, believe the evidence: re-investigate, fix, re-verify, and report the disagreement honestly.
4. Where subagents are unavailable, do a deliberate fresh-pass review yourself and say plainly that no independent review was possible.

Read `~/.cursor/skills/independent-review/SKILL.md` (or `.cursor/skills/independent-review/SKILL.md`).
